<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Esquipulas Peace Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1987</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Esquipulas II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Esquipulas Peace Agreement, or Esquipulas II, was signed on 7 August 1987 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala-city">Guatemala City</a> by the presidents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>, Honduras, Nicaragua and Costa Rica, following a first summit at Esquipulas in Guatemala in 1986. Based on a plan by the Costa Rican president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscar-arias">Óscar Arias</a>, it committed the governments to ceasefires, national reconciliation, democratisation and an end to support for insurgents, opening the way to peace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>.</p></div>
